<!-- Otras tarjetas de info -->

<div class="w-full flex justify-center py-24">
  <div class="flex flex-nowrap gap-8">

    <div class="w-72 bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl">
      <div class="h-24 bg-green-900 px-5 relative flex items-center">
        <div class="text-white font-semibold text-xl">Proper Watering</div>
        <div
          class="absolute bottom-[-14px] left-5 w-8 h-8 bg-yellow-400 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">
          01</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pt-7 px-5 pb-6 text-sm font-bold">Water sparingly. Let the soil dry out completely between waterings.
      </div>
      <div class="pt-1/2 px-5 pb-6 text-sm">Tip: Overwatering is the most common cause of succulent death.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="w-72 bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl">
      <div class="h-24 bg-gray-600 px-5 relative flex items-center">
        <div class="text-white font-semibold text-xl">Soil and Nutrition</div>
        <div
          class="absolute bottom-[-14px] left-5 w-8 h-8 bg-yellow-400 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">
          02</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pt-7 px-5 pb-6 text-sm font-bold">Use well-draining soil, preferably a cactus or succulent mix.</div>
      <div class="pt-1/2 px-5 pb-6 text-sm">Tip: Fertilize lightly during the growing season (spring and summer) with a
        balanced, diluted fertilizer.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="w-72 bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl">
      <div class="h-24 bg-green-900 px-5 relative flex items-center">
        <div class="text-white font-semibold text-xl">Pruning and Cleaning</div>
        <div
          class="absolute bottom-[-14px] left-5 w-8 h-8 bg-yellow-400 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">
          03</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pt-7 px-5 pb-6 text-sm font-bold">Regular pruning helps succulents stay healthy and visually
        appealing. Remove dried, dead, or damaged leaves to prevent rot and pest infestations.</div>
      <div class="pt-1/2 px-5 pb-6 text-sm">Tip: Use clean, sharp scissors or tweezers to gently trim away unwanted
        growth.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="w-72 bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl">
      <div class="h-24 bg-gray-600 px-5 relative flex items-center">
        <div class="text-white font-semibold text-xl">Environment and Placement</div>
        <div
          class="absolute bottom-[-14px] left-5 w-8 h-8 bg-yellow-400 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">
          04</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pt-7 px-5 pb-6 text-sm font-bold">Succulents prefer warm, dry environments with good airflow.</div>
      <div class="pt-1/2 px-5 pb-6 text-sm">Tip: Avoid placing them in overly humid areas like bathrooms or kitchens, as
        excess moisture can lead to rot. Ideal spots include sunny windowsills, shelves near natural light, or outdoor
        patios with partial shade.</div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
<hr class="pb-24 mx-10 border-t-4 border-white border-opacity-40">
<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
  <div>
